1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:07,640
You think you've explored medicine. In reality, you're standing in the parking lot of Disney World bragging about how fun

2
00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:13,950
the pavement is. You've taken pictures of the asphalt. You've written dissertations about the parking stripes.

3
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:24,310
You've never gone inside. After a century of pharmacology, most beneficial effects of molecules on diseases remain unexplored.

4
00:00:24,940 --> 00:00:33,820
Not because biology is constrained. Because clinical trials are slow, expensive, and run by people who think "urgency" is

5
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:41,140
a type of perfume. Here's the math. It's painful but brief, like a flu shot administered by someone who hates you.

6
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:51,520
Your Tiny Sandbox. Here is everything humanity considers "medicine" after five thousand years of civilization: There are

7
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:59,800
twenty thousand prescription products approved in the U.S. Sounds impressive until you realize most are just "Tylenol, but

8
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:05,600
blue." These products contain only one thousand six hundred and fifty unique ingredients.

9
00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:09,900
That is fewer ingredients than a decent French bakery uses.

10
00:01:10,860 --> 00:01:15,700
Seven thousand five hundred investigational drugs have passed Phase One globally.

11
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:25,760
Progress! The F.D.A. generally recognized as safe, or G.R.A.S., list contains six hundred and thirty-five substances.

12
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:30,880
These are things you could eat right now without dying. Low bar.

13
00:01:31,280 --> 00:01:39,760
Still useful. Total unique compounds humanity knows are safe-ish: nine thousand five hundred compounds.

14
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:44,940
That's it. That's your entire medicine cabinet after five millennia.

15
00:01:45,020 --> 00:01:52,580
The Target List (Ways Your Body Breaks). The International Classification of Diseases, or I.C.D.

16
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:57,780
ten, lists fourteen thousand ways your meat can malfunction.

17
00:01:58,520 --> 00:02:03,100
Humanity's most comprehensive to-do list, and you're ignoring it.

18
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:09,699
After consolidation, there are one thousand trial-relevant diseases worth actually fixing.

19
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:15,640
The Math You're Ignoring. Take your nine thousand five hundred safe compounds.

20
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:24,260
Multiply by one thousand diseases. This gives you the "Combinatorial Space," which is fancy talk for "stuff you could test

21
00:02:24,260 --> 00:02:32,180
tomorrow if you weren't busy filling out forms." Nine thousand five hundred compounds times one thousand diseases equals

22
00:02:32,180 --> 00:02:36,800
nine point five million plausible drug-condition combinations.

23
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:44,640
What You've Actually Tested. There are one thousand seven hundred and fifty unique approved drug-disease pairings.

24
00:02:45,260 --> 00:02:53,100
That is your entire medical canon. Thirty percent of drugs gain at least one new indication after initial approval.

25
00:02:53,820 --> 00:03:00,820
The rest never get a second date. Let's be generous and say you tested ten times as many things that failed.

26
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:07,700
(You did. You learned nothing from them.). Total tested: thirty-two thousand five hundred relationships.

27
00:03:08,340 --> 00:03:12,920
The Scorecard. Thirty-two thousand five hundred relationships tested divided by nine point five million possibilities equals

28
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:22,780
zero point three four two percent. where: Humanity has explored about a third of one percent of the theoretically testable

29
00:03:22,780 --> 00:03:29,620
drug-disease space. You are the detective who searched one drawer and declared the case cold.

30
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:36,300
It's like reading the first page of *War and Peace* and writing a book report called "It's About a Party."

31
00:03:37,220 --> 00:03:43,280
Technically accurate. Cosmically insufficient. Is The Untested Stuff Useful?

32
00:03:43,660 --> 00:03:47,780
You might argue, "Maybe the other ninety-nine point seven percent is useless!".

33
00:03:48,640 --> 00:03:54,880
Biology would like a word. Mapping three hundred and fifty thousand plus clinical trials showed that only twelve percent

34
00:03:54,880 --> 00:04:02,080
of the human interactome has ever been targeted by drugs. You're ignoring eighty-eight percent of your own biology.

35
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:07,240
It's like having a one hundred-room mansion and living exclusively in the bathroom.

36
00:04:07,620 --> 00:04:13,900
Drugs are messy. They hit multiple targets. F.D.A.-approved drugs often bind to things you didn't intend.

37
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:19,540
This means "side effects" are frequently "cures for something else" that nobody bothered to notice.

38
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:28,420
Sildenafil was developed for chest pain. It failed. Its "side effect" became Viagra, then got repurposed again for pulmonary

39
00:04:28,420 --> 00:04:36,360
hypertension. Thalidomide was pulled for causing birth defects; its immunomodulatory "side effects" turned out to treat

40
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:42,900
multiple myeloma. Two drugs. Three accidental cures. Zero systematic searches.

41
00:04:43,540 --> 00:04:48,940
You keep finding cures by tripping over them in hallways. Imagine if you opened a door on purpose.

42
00:04:49,840 --> 00:04:56,090
Diseases cluster on shared biological networks. Arthritis and Alzheimer's share biological pathways.

43
00:04:56,240 --> 00:05:02,260
Lithium was prescribed for gout in the eighteen hundreds; decades later, it turned out to be the gold standard treatment

44
00:05:02,460 --> 00:05:08,280
for bipolar disorder. Nobody connected the dots because nobody was drawing lines between diseases.

45
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:14,960
The drug that treats your grandfather's inflammation might fix your grandmother's neurodegeneration.

46
00:05:15,580 --> 00:05:21,000
You won't find out, because testing it would require paperwork that takes longer than Grandma has left.

47
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:30,210
The Universe is Big. You Are Small. Estimated ten to the twenty-third power to ten to the sixtieth power drug-like molecules.

48
00:05:31,060 --> 00:05:35,460
That's more candidates than there are atoms in your body. Or stars in the galaxy.

49
00:05:35,900 --> 00:05:43,680
Or excuses from your regulatory agencies. ZINC-twenty-two contains tens of billions of purchasable virtual molecules.

50
00:05:44,580 --> 00:05:52,040
You could order them online. You haven't. You have made less than ten to the negative fortieth power of possible molecules.

51
00:05:53,040 --> 00:06:00,060
Tested divided by possible is approximately ten to the negative twentieth to ten to the negative fiftieth power.

52
00:06:00,820 --> 00:06:08,280
Effectively zero. You haven't even started. This is like exploring Earth by looking at one grain of sand on one beach in

53
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:12,080
New Jersey, then declaring you've "seen the world." You haven't.

54
00:06:12,660 --> 00:06:16,760
You've seen a grain of sand. In New Jersey. Why You Are Still Sick.

55
00:06:17,760 --> 00:06:23,140
It's not because science is hard. It's because you've built a system that is allergic to answers.

56
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:32,540
One. Trials Cost Too Much. A typical Phase two to three randomized controlled trial, or R.C.T., costs thirty to one hundred

57
00:06:32,540 --> 00:06:36,860
million dollars (Median cost per patient forty-one thousand dollars).

58
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:42,060
At that price, you only test "sure things." Safe bets. Boring bets.

59
00:06:42,780 --> 00:06:49,720
Bets that don't cure cancer. Clinical trials are a velvet-rope nightclub where the bouncer is a regulatory agency and the

60
00:06:49,880 --> 00:06:53,740
cover charge is a hundred million dollars. Two. Herd Mentality.

61
00:06:54,940 --> 00:06:59,920
Trials overwhelmingly test the same few biological targets due to preferential attachment dynamics.

62
00:07:01,220 --> 00:07:04,770
Everyone studies what everyone else studies because that's how you get grants.

63
00:07:05,400 --> 00:07:11,000
It's like if every explorer only went to France because France already had good reviews on TripAdvisor.

64
00:07:11,400 --> 00:07:15,720
Meanwhile, undiscovered continents full of cures sit there, undiscovered.

65
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:26,010
Three. No Profit. Most molecules have no patent. No patent equals no one hundred million dollar trial equals no approval.

66
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:33,340
Metformin, a diabetes drug from the nineteen fifties, shows persistent signals for reducing cancer risk and extending lifespan.

67
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:42,000
It costs pennies. It's off-patent. The trial to prove it works for aging (Targeting Aging with Metformin, or TAME) spent

68
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:47,680
years begging for funding because no pharmaceutical company will bankroll a drug they can't monopolize.

69
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:53,170
The molecule that saves your life has to make money first. If it can't, it won't.

70
00:07:53,700 --> 00:08:02,060
You die. Quarterly earnings go up. Four. Neglect. If you have a rare disease with no market, you don't get a drug.

71
00:08:02,580 --> 00:08:08,580
Your cells malfunction in an unprofitable way. The invisible hand of the market has weighed your life against quarterly

72
00:08:08,580 --> 00:08:13,000
earnings and found you wanting. Sorry about your death. It was a business decision.

73
00:08:14,180 --> 00:08:21,480
How Long to Explore Everything? At the current pace of three thousand three hundred trials per year, how long would it take

74
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:27,800
to systematically test therapeutic possibilities? Tier 1: Single Compounds (Most Conservative).

75
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:36,380
Testing every known safe compound against every major disease: Nine point five million combinations divided by three thousand

76
00:08:36,380 --> 00:08:40,960
three hundred trials per year equals two thousand eight hundred and eighty years.

77
00:08:41,700 --> 00:08:47,460
That's almost two thousand eight hundred and eighty years to explore compounds we already know are safe.

78
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:51,260
By that math, we won't finish until the year five thousand.

79
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:59,600
Tier 2: Combination Therapies (Still Defensible). Modern medicine increasingly relies on multi-drug cocktails.

80
00:09:00,100 --> 00:09:05,620
Oncology, H.I.V., cardiology, psychiatry: all routinely use drug combinations.

81
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:11,540
So the real question isn't "does this one drug work?" It's "which combinations work?"

82
00:09:12,480 --> 00:09:19,980
Testing pairwise combinations of safe compounds: Forty-five point one billion combinations divided by three thousand three

83
00:09:19,980 --> 00:09:25,040
hundred trials per year equals thirteen point seven million years.

84
00:09:25,620 --> 00:09:33,040
That's longer than Homo sapiens has existed as a species. And that's using only compounds with established safety data,

85
00:09:33,500 --> 00:09:37,850
testing only pairs. Not triplets. God help you if you want to try triplets.

86
00:09:38,900 --> 00:09:46,960
Tier 3: The Full Chemical Universe (Illustrative). Beyond known compounds lies the chemical space of ten to the twenty-third

87
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:54,280
power to ten to the sixtieth power drug-like molecules. At current trial capacity, exploring even the synthesizable fraction

88
00:09:54,280 --> 00:10:01,000
would take longer than the universe has existed. The universe is thirteen point eight billion years old.

89
00:10:01,620 --> 00:10:06,730
You need more time than that. To test pills. Pills that already exist.

90
00:10:06,960 --> 00:10:11,110
We haven't even started. But Won't We Run Out of Easy Discoveries?

91
00:10:11,980 --> 00:10:16,760
Some will argue "diminishing returns": the more we search, the harder each new discovery becomes.

92
00:10:17,180 --> 00:10:21,780
This assumes we've already picked the low-hanging fruit. We haven't picked *any* fruit.

93
00:10:22,280 --> 00:10:24,920
We're still in the parking lot arguing about whether fruit exists.

94
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:30,660
Diminishing returns only kicks in after you've explored a significant fraction of the space.

95
00:10:31,280 --> 00:10:38,120
At less than one percent explored, every trial teaches you something new about human biology, improving your ability to

96
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:42,740
predict what works next. Learning compounds. Depletion is negligible.

97
00:10:43,260 --> 00:10:47,440
You are nowhere near the bottom of the barrel because you have not yet located the barrel.

98
00:10:48,420 --> 00:10:56,280
The math: even with weak learning, diminishing returns only matters after exploring roughly thirty-seven percent of therapeutic

99
00:10:56,280 --> 00:11:05,100
space. For combination therapies, that crossover is over five million years away at current pace (thirty-seven percent of

100
00:11:05,100 --> 00:11:11,340
forty-five point one billion combinations at three thousand three hundred trials per year).

101
00:11:11,960 --> 00:11:15,240
You cannot have diminishing returns when you've barely started looking.

102
00:11:16,060 --> 00:11:25,020
See the formal analysis for the equations. The Fix. The Oxford RECOVERY Trial (COVID nineteen) proved that large-scale pragmatic

103
00:11:25,020 --> 00:11:31,520
trials can run for approximately five hundred dollars and deliver results in less than one hundred days.

104
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:36,920
Five hundred dollars versus forty-one thousand dollars. Read those numbers again.

105
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:45,380
One of them is the reason people are dying. With a decentralized F.D.A., trial capacity increases by twelve point three

106
00:11:45,380 --> 00:11:54,400
times: Nine point five million combinations divided by forty thousand seven hundred trials per year equals two hundred and

107
00:11:54,400 --> 00:12:00,120
thirty-four years. Still a long time, but at least it's a number with fewer digits than a phone book.

108
00:12:00,900 --> 00:12:07,280
And the first few decades would capture the highest-value discoveries (the low-hanging fruit that current trial scarcity

109
00:12:07,280 --> 00:12:10,300
forces you to ignore while people die in the waiting room).

110
00:12:11,280 --> 00:12:18,600
More importantly, your decentralized F.D.A. builds *permanent infrastructure* for systematic therapeutic exploration.

111
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:25,780
The goal isn't to "finish." It's to stop leaving cures on the table while you form subcommittees to discuss whether to form

112
00:12:25,780 --> 00:12:30,650
committees to review the proposal to consider them. The Bottom Line.

113
00:12:31,060 --> 00:12:38,400
Humanity has empirically tested less than zero point three four two percent of the drug-disease relationships that can be

114
00:12:38,520 --> 00:12:47,200
tested using existing safe compounds. If you include the larger chemical universe, humanity has explored roughly one-quadrillionth

115
00:12:48,080 --> 00:12:53,560
to one-quintillionth of what is possible (ten to the negative twelve to ten to the negative fifty).

116
00:12:54,780 --> 00:12:59,260
There are numbers so small that mathematicians get depressed looking at them.

117
00:12:59,500 --> 00:13:05,060
These are those numbers. The overwhelming majority of therapeutic potential remains untouched.

118
00:13:05,660 --> 00:13:10,700
Not because cures are impossible. Because trials are too expensive and too slow.

119
00:13:11,440 --> 00:13:19,200
A decentralized, automated pragmatic trial system is the only route to systematically explore the remaining ninety-nine

120
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:27,820
point nine nine nine percent of medical space. You're not in the parking lot because there's nothing inside Disney World.

121
00:13:27,840 --> 00:13:34,060
You're in the parking lot because the entrance fee is one hundred million dollars and requires seventeen years of paperwork.

122
00:13:34,740 --> 00:13:38,730
People are dying in the parking lot. The rides are right there.

123
00:13:38,980 --> 00:13:44,000
You can hear the screaming. (Fun screaming. Cure screaming.).

124
00:13:44,640 --> 00:13:47,700
The cures are inside. Open the gate.
